 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 545632,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "New Mexico was admitted as the 47th state on January 6, 1912. Before New Mexico joined the union, the U.S. population was approximately 76,000,000 and the House of Representatives had 391 seats. The new state had a population of approximately 300,000. Use this information to estimate the original standard divisor to the nearest hundred, the new population, the new house size, and the number of seats New Mexico should receive.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{Original Standard Divisor}} \\approx \\frac{{76,000,000}}{{391}} \\approx 194,400\">&lt;{\\text{Original Standard Divisor}} \\approx \\frac{{76,000,000}}{{391}} \\approx 194,400&gt;</span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{New Population}} \\approx 76,000,000 + 300,000 = 76,300,000\">\n&lt;{\\text{New Population}} \\approx 76,000,000 + 300,000 = 76,300,000&gt;</span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{New House Size}} \\approx \\frac{{{\\text{76,300,000}}}}{{194,400}} \\approx 392\"></span></p>\n<p>There are <span data-math=\"392 - 391 = 1\">&lt;392 - 391 = 1&gt;</span> new seats to be apportioned to New Mexico.</p> \n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{Standard Divisor = }}\\frac{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}{{{\\text{House Size}}}} = \\frac{{{\\text{76,000,000}}}}{{{\\text{391 seats}}}} \\approx 194,400{\\text{ people per seat}}\"></span></p>\n<p>New total population <span data-math=\"{\\text{ =  76,000,000  +  300,000  =  76,300,000}}\"></span> people.</p>\n<p>To estimate the new house size, rearrange the equation for the standard divisor.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"{\\text{Standard Divisor = }}\\frac{{{\\text{Total Population}}}}{{{\\text{House Size}}}}\"></span></td>\n<td>Multiply.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\left( {{\\text{House Size}}} \\right){\\text{ }}\\left( {{\\text{Standard Divisor}}} \\right){\\text{ = Total Population}}\"></span></td>\n<td>Divide.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{New House Size = }}\\frac{{{\\text{New Total Population}}}}{{{\\text{Standard Divisor}}}} = \\frac{{76,300,000}}{{194,400{\\text{ people per seat}}}} \\approx 392{\\text{ seats}}\"></span></p>\n<p>New House Size – Old House Size = 392 – 391 = 1 new seat to be apportioned to New Mexico.</p>\n<p>The original standard divisor: <span data-math=\"194,400{\\text{ people per seat}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The new population: 76,300,000 people</p>\n<p>The new house size: 392 seats</p>\n<p>The number of seats New Mexico should receive: 1 seat</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
